WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.030
When a dead man rises.

00:00:02.439 --> 00:00:05.399
How does he come to bear with his unnatural existence?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.920
For every story deserves an ending, and without one what is there to treasure?

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:16.000
So he looks for purpose in his undeath, a notoriously difficult task.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.660
But, even accursed undead want to believe they're special, it seems.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.869
First he joins a legion, united in their resolve. A pack of wolves,

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:36.058
sworn to do battle with the dark where ever it arises. The same dark they say that is responsible for the curse of the undead.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.349
Battling against horrors and monsters like heroes past.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.819
Battling themselves, for that is where the true corruption lies.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:51.360
Until one day the man turns coat and leaves, unable to bear the burden.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.980
For even in undeath, Hawkwood feared his mortality.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:03.120
He clutched a shield close to his chest, unlike his brothers and sisters. He fought with a blade designed to catch and deflect mortal strikes.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.640
Hawkwood the craven; the crestfallen.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:12.500
However, by nature of definition, it is the coward who is capable of the highest heroism.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.000
For his obstacles, are the greatest of all.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.050
"Are you the next Monarch? Or merely a pawn of fate?"

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:28.140
He believed that he could still be a hero. A champion to banish the dark with the light of the first flame.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.999
Someone worthy of a throne, a place in this world that is engraved with his name.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.999
Hawkwood, an undead worthy of fire.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:44.699
But again, he failed. A nameless accursed that undead. Unfit even to be cinder, and so he becomes ash.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:53.200
When a dead man rises he becomes his failure. Forced to know that his best was not nearly enough.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.968
"Ah, another one, roused from the sleep of death."

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:02.919
"Well, you're not alone. We unkindlled are worthless."

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:05.979
"We can't even die right..."

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:14.199
"Gives me conniptions. And they'd have us seek the lords of cinder and return them to their molding Thrones?"

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:20.768
"But we are talking true legends, with the mettle to link the fire."

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.010
"We're not fit to lick their boots."

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.900
"Don't you think?"

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.320
Each of them a man who actually became a fire linking King.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:39.900
"Not for virtue, but for might. Such as a lord, I suppose."

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:45.040
"But here I ask, do we have a sodding chance?"

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.800
How could ashen failures possibly hope to convince four Lords to listen to them?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.260
Well, if the Lord's will not return to their thrones themselves.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.720
Let them return as cinders.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.440
"You offed the Lords of Cinder, the Undead Legion..."

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.440
"So that's how they're delivered to their thrones?"

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.220
"I pity the sorry Souls..."

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.960
""Is that really, Lordships last reward?"

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.980
It finally hit him, the absurdity of it all.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:25.980
"The poor wretched souls. Be they Lord or legend the curse shows no mercy..."

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.400
"What a sham..."

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:33.280
And if Kings could not escape their fate? Well, then they were no lesser than he.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.760
So what did he have to fear? Nothing.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:42.140
"I'm a deserter, I know. But I've still plenty of fight in me!"

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.480
First, he followed the wolf. Then he was scarred by fire.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:53.700
Finally, he finds the courage to pursue another calling. The calling of those who seek to exist outside of the cycle.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.680
But to be alive, is to be vulnerable. And even the fiery gods, no exception to that rule.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.680
No, the Apostles of the Dragon seek another plane of existence.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:10.780
One which transcends life. And we, possess one of their relics.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:20.020
"Oh, you've returned. I was hoping to see y'. That crestfallen arsehole, he handed me this."

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.720
"He's changed a great deal since he left this place."

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.260
"Graven of face, he asked me to give it y' "

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:36.380
It was a challenge. This time he fights for something else completely, without a shield to protect his own self.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.080
"Ah, there you are..."

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.420
"Well, I've decided to stop running from my fate."

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.340
"Loathe me. All you like,"

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.700
"I shall take what makes you Dragon."

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.520
"This shall be no petty theft."

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:04.020
"As the true dragon I shall take what is rightfully mine."

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:11.540
"Ah, I should have know... Enough, you fool!"

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:31.240
"Oh, be as bloody mad as you like... Trapped within your wretched clast..."

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.440
"You are, a dragon."

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.220
"More dragon, than I."

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.700
"A deserter could hope for no better place to die..."

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:55.860
His name was Hawkwood, the last remaining warrior of the undead legion.

